# WFORMTN.KEY - view mode: the item form opens with the focus on its tab
# strip, which a letter of no tab leaves where it is; Tab visits the
# read-only edit controls of the page shown, free text longer than its
# box (Part of, Tags), the record buttons, Close and Edit, then those of
# the identity row (Maker), and Enter there closes the dialog, saving
# nothing.  In the form of every type, whose values are all text, Tab
# goes between the strip and Close; Ctrl+Tab shows Notes, Tab reaches
# the memo, which takes nothing typed, and Enter closes the dialog;
# TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/WFORMTN.SNP.
K F4
S ITEM
T x
S TYPED
K TAB
S PARTOF
K TAB
S TAGS
K TAB
S PARTS
K TAB TAB TAB TAB
S CLOSE
K TAB
S EDIT
K TAB
S MAKER
K ENTER
S ITEMEND
K F6
S ALL
K TAB
S ALLCLOSE
K TAB
S STRIP
K CTRL-TAB
S NOTES
K TAB
S MEMO
T x
S TYPEDX
K ENTER
S ALLEND
